    description: "Found by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (dev 95c0ff7b93): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier confirmed it by reading the code itself (a repro where stated). Severity is not asserted; impact not measured on the corpus.\n\n- swift.py: Two function-local `struct Inner { init(x: Int) {} ; deinit {} ; func go() {} }`, one in `func f` and one in `func g` of one file, share their constructor AND deinit stable_ids, while their struct and `go` ids differ -- evidence: `analyze_swift` on a scratch repo printed\n\nNot asserted: that the fix is the one sketched above, or that no other language has the same shape."  # 6056
